{"ts":"2026-08-13T08:46:47.326Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ebf2cca0e1c37e7b3d988ef","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-hnc9w7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.229","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-13T08:46:47.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Batch executed for three of four codes, changelog effect measured first rather than assumed.\n\nBefore: 11 findings; nodes 2458 (missing_nodes 3); edges 12116; tracker-context-quality verdict pass.\n\nExecuted:\n- legacy_duplicate_edge 8 -> 0. Collapsed 8 reciprocal child rows onto the canonical parent edge each child already stored: pm-7t04 (5 rows: 0nia, 1265, 8rjn, b8rf, g2nd) and pm-v7dj (3 rows: aqat, jauk, ze5g). Lossless, because parent and child are declared inverses and every child stores the parent spelling.\n- missing_reference_terminal 3 -> 0. Removed pm-1p2u's related row to the non-existent pm-0wm0, and cleared two legacy free-text blocked_by scalars that were never item ids (pm-lty 'backlog-sequencing', pm-zdec 'design-review').\n- legacy_no_blocker_sentinel 98 -> 0. Cleared the retired no-active-blocker scalar on all 98 holders; blocker state now derives from real edges only.\n\nAfter: 8 findings, all legacy_ordering_cycle; nodes 2455; edges 12105.\n\nChangelog effect, measured not assumed: regeneration diff was 15 lines, all intra-section reordering of the four touched closed items within their own already-published release sections. No item entered [Unreleased]; no section gained or lost an item. All 98 sentinel holders and all 4 touched items carry a release value, which is the field the generator buckets by. Filed as pm-71v4l9: the closed_at rule this item's body relies on over-counts the risky population by 4.4x (1475 vs the real 337).\n\nFourth code not executed, and it is not a scheduling choice: the root cause of all 8 cycles is now known (26 holders storing a scalar blocked_by X together with a contradicting structured row X,blocks; full list on pm-xvt7ps), the repair is mechanical, and removing those 26 rows takes edges to 12079 against graph-edges-floor 12103 at block enforcement. Recorded blocked_by pm-mfvsng."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T08:46:47.326Z"}],"before_hash":"e488ed029ae18b7045a0fb64a7e7d0445049eacb2561297b5c3ee1651c8d3025","after_hash":"3ea715f560b281a68ab62e6b61d853417532b4dfb132b0ea386830e920eee2c2","item_hash_version":2}
{"ts":"2026-08-13T09:00:19.489Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ebf2cca0e1c37e7b3d988ef","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-hnc9w7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-hnc9w7","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.229","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-13T09:00:19.489Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"CI hardening attempted and blocked, recorded so the earned state is not mistaken for an enforced one.\n\nThe three ceilings this batch drove to zero are still declared at their pre-batch values: graph-finding-legacy-duplicate-edge-ceiling 8, graph-finding-legacy-no-blocker-sentinel-ceiling 98, graph-finding-missing-reference-terminal-ceiling 3. Tightening them to 0 is what converts this batch from a one-off cleanup into a regression gate, and it is the whole reason the batch is worth doing.\n\nEvery attempt fails: 'Workspace history state for assurance.json changed outside the audited mutation path.' The refusal is correct and predates this session — the committed registry carries two loosenings that the append-only workspace stream never recorded (health-telemetry-zero block to warn, graph-outcome-reachable-floor 2438 to 2434), both written by commit 0132ed74b. Filed as pm-h06944 with the full replay diff. Until it is reconciled the assurance registry is frozen for all writes, including no-op re-puts.\n\nSo the batch's state is: three of four legacy codes cleaned to zero in the data, zero of three earned ceilings tightened in the declarations. A regression that re-introduces sentinels, duplicate parent/child spellings or dangling references would still pass CI today. This item should not close until the ceilings are at 0, which makes it dependent on pm-h06944 as well as pm-mfvsng."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T09:00:19.489Z"}],"before_hash":"3ea715f560b281a68ab62e6b61d853417532b4dfb132b0ea386830e920eee2c2","after_hash":"9cc1be1bef4fb6a3859e882c3ec357c2ee5ffbd76f08e0b772866296a4b4bf45","item_hash_version":2}
